---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="API" description="Machine-readable access to the OpenAgent.bot registry." path="/api">
  <div class="page-shell"><div class="page-grid">
    <section class="page-section"><span class="kicker">Public API / v1</span><h1 class="page-title">Machine-readable registry access</h1><p class="lede">Read-only entity, statistics and knowledge endpoints with attributed facts and explicit unknowns.</p></section>
    <section class="page-section"><article class="prose">
      <h2>List entities</h2><p><code>GET /api/v1/entities.json</code></p><p>Query parameters: <code>q</code>, <code>domain</code>, <code>layer</code>, <code>kind</code>, <code>use_case</code>, <code>interface</code>, <code>openness</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>limit</code>, <code>offset</code>. Domain describes the ecosystem field, <code>layer</code> separates robot platforms, intelligence and stack, and kind describes the artifact form. Use cases are cross-cutting filters, for example <a href="/api/v1/entities.json?use_case=sim-to-real"><code>use_case=sim-to-real</code></a>. Interface values are <code>cli</code>, <code>api</code>, <code>mcp</code> and <code>sdk</code>; these describe documented access, not independent certification.</p>
      <h2>Entity documents</h2><p><code>GET /project/:slug.json</code> · <code>GET /project/:slug.md</code></p><p>Canonical JSON and compact Markdown representations are generated from the same dossier as the human-readable project page. JSON includes attributed facts, use cases, relationships, tool interfaces, source-labelled metric snapshots and reviewed resource manifests. Resource revisions and Git blob hashes identify inspected files; they are not a live file mirror. Package versions and downloads use <code>npm.*</code> facts; stable releases use <code>github_release.*</code>. <code>npm_downloads_30d</code> is package activity, not model downloads or user count.</p>
      <h2>Registry statistics</h2><p><code>GET /api/v1/stats.json</code></p>
      <h2>Knowledge v0.1 preview: strict search</h2>
      <p><a href="/api/knowledge/v1/search.json?interface=mcp&access=read-only&authentication=none"><code>GET /api/knowledge/v1/search.json?interface=mcp&amp;access=read-only&amp;authentication=none</code></a></p>
      <p>Required: <code>interface=cli|api|mcp|sdk</code>. Optional: <code>access=read-only|local-write-opt-in|read-write</code>, <code>authentication=none|required|optional</code>, <code>verification=documented|tested</code>, <code>require_fresh=true|false</code>, <code>version_id</code>, <code>domain=agent|robotics|shared</code>, <code>project</code> (slug), <code>q</code> (literal name/summary substring), <code>limit</code> (1–20), <code>cursor</code>. Default verification is documented; freshness is not required unless requested. Conditions must match the same interface. Domain membership is not runtime or hardware compatibility.</p>
      <p>Only published interface declarations are searched. Unknown claims cannot satisfy a condition. Follow <code>nextCursor</code>, even on an empty page: each request examines at most 50 candidates. An exhausted search does not establish absence outside the recorded declarations. Search pagination is a live keyset, not a frozen snapshot.</p>
      <h2>Knowledge v0.1 preview: small project sections</h2>
      <p><code>GET /api/knowledge/v1/project.json?slug=vgpu</code> returns an overview. Use <code>section=interfaces|resources|openness|fields|facts</code>; interfaces/resources accept an exact local <code>id</code>. Discover fact keys with <code>section=fields</code>, then retrieve a value with <code>section=facts&amp;fact_key=...</code>. The field index omits values; its status describes only the top-level claim, not unknown nested properties. Section lists accept <code>limit</code> (1–20) and <code>cursor</code>. A changed record returns 409 during pagination. The <code>evidence</code> dictionary resolves per-response evidence references; resource versions retain their own digests and terms.</p>
      <h2>Knowledge v0.1 preview: recorded history</h2>
      <p>For known-project fact lookups, follow the overview's <code>links.fields</code>, then the relevant field's <code>valueUrl</code>. A project-only search without <code>interface</code> is invalid.</p>
      <p><code>GET /api/knowledge/v1/history.json?slug=vgpu</code>. Optional: <code>since</code> (inclusive timezone-qualified ISO timestamp), <code>fact_key</code>, <code>limit</code> (default 5, maximum 20), <code>cursor</code>. Continue with the same filters. The append window excludes later ledger appends but is not a transaction snapshot. Times are registry detection times, not upstream effective times. Values over 4,096 bytes are explicitly marked <code>truncated</code>; full-value export is not yet provided.</p>
      <p>Knowledge endpoints accept GET only, return 400 for unsupported/duplicate parameters, 404 for missing public records, 413 for oversized responses and 503 for unavailable storage/projections. They use <code>Cache-Control: no-store</code>. Legacy v1 filters are unchanged and do not support these stricter constraints.</p>
      <p><code>firstRecordedAt</code> is the earliest retained observation insertion time, independent of <code>since</code>. New fact selections produce <code>created</code>; explicitly reviewed corrections produce <code>corrected</code> with a reason and old/new evidence references. No missing past events are fabricated. Legacy change JSON retains its base event kind; correction annotations are on this Knowledge history endpoint.</p>
      <p><strong>Not execution permission:</strong> access labels describe documented capabilities, not the active configuration or a safety guarantee. A local write-opt-in interface may default to read-only. Source references are not necessarily callable endpoints; commands are inert text. Documented is not tested, and source sync time does not establish field freshness. No tool, shader, policy or robot is executed by these APIs.</p>
      <h2>Response policy</h2><p>Responses include cache headers and canonical project URLs. Entity documents expose each current fact's source and observation date; bulk observation-history exports are not yet available. Repository metrics may refresh automatically while product specifications and resource manifests retain their own review dates.</p>
    </article></section>
  </div></div>
</BaseLayout>
